# Final Project 

#### At the beginning of this module, students were introduced to the final project: a multi-page digital magazine that serves as the culmination of Unit 1.

#### As students progress through the lessons, they practice the same tools and design strategies they will apply in the final project.

#### Throughout the unit, students refine their ideas and drafts by considering how real users will experience their work.

<img src="https://images.code.org/0fa53a5cbf5480e4c10f9f2bc406506f-image-1765910932701.png" alt="generic website" width="350px" style="border-radius:10px; float:right; margin: 20px 0 40px 40px;">

## Multi-page web application
#### In the final project, students step into the role of web designers to create a multi-page digital magazine for a fictional user or community.

#### They define their target audience and brand identity, plan layouts for key pages such as the home and article pages, and use AI in Guide Mode to generate the HTML and CSS that bring their designs to life.


## You did it! 

#### You’ve now practiced using the tools to build this project while getting an overview of much of the Unit 1 content. This module is designed to give you a strong head start as you prepare to teach the unit.

## Want to try more? 

#### If you’d like to try to complete the full project, open the link in a new tab and return to it after finishing this module.

